{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a stitch task (Task ID: 5310) titled \"[stitch] cmd/sha256sum core hashing implementation (srd032 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\". The task requires creating `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` — a SHA-256 checksum utility that follows the exact same pattern as the existing `cmd/md5sum/main.go`, substituting only the hash function (crypto/sha256), algorithm name (\"SHA256\"), and digest length (32). The task is part of an automated code generation pipeline (cobbler orchestrator) and explicitly prohibits git commands, filesystem exploration, or scope creep.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU sha256sum utility\n   - Shared `pkg/hashutil` library providing `HashConfig`, `DigestFiles`, `FormatGNU`, `VerifyChecksums`, `ComputeDigest`, `ParseChecksumLine`, `FormatBSDTag`\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling in all cmd/ utilities\n   - Differential testing pattern against GNU reference binaries (gsha256sum)\n   - GNU two-space format for text mode, asterisk format for binary mode\n   - HashConfig struct: `{Algorithm string, NewHash func() hash.Hash, DigestLen int}`\n   - Copyright header requirement: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `cmd/md5sum/main.go` (READ - reference implementation to follow exactly):\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"crypto/md5\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n     \n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         cfg := hashutil.HashConfig{\n             Algorithm: \"MD5\",\n             NewHash:   md5.New,\n             DigestLen: 16,\n         }\n         if opts.check {\n             checkOpts := hashutil.CheckOptions{\n                 Warn:   opts.warn,\n                 Quiet:  opts.quiet,\n                 Status: opts.status,\n             }\n             exitCode := 0\n             for _, f := range files {\n                 ok, err := hashutil.VerifyChecksums(f, cfg, checkOpts, os.Stdout, os.Stderr)\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"md5sum: %s\\n\", err)\n                     exitCode = 1\n                 } else if !ok {\n                     exitCode = 1\n                 }\n             }\n             os.Exit(exitCode)\n         }\n         os.Exit(hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n     }\n     \n     type options struct {\n         binary bool\n         tag    bool\n         check  bool\n         warn   bool\n         quiet  bool\n         status bool\n     }\n     \n     func parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string) {\n         var opts options\n         var files []string\n         i := 0\n         for i < len(args) {\n             arg := args[i]\n             if arg == \"--\" {\n                 files = append(files, args[i+1:]...)\n                 break\n             }\n             if handled, advance := parseLongFlag(arg, &opts); handled {\n                 i += advance\n                 continue\n             }\n             if arg == \"-\" || !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") {\n                 files = append(files, arg)\n                 i++\n                 continue\n             }\n             i += parseShortFlags(arg[1:], &opts)\n         }\n         return opts, files\n     }\n     \n     func parseLongFlag(arg string, opts *options) (bool, int) {\n         if !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n             return false, 0\n         }\n         switch arg {\n         case \"--binary\":\n             opts.binary = true\n         case \"--text\":\n             opts.binary = false\n         case \"--tag\":\n             opts.tag = true\n         case \"--check\":\n             opts.check = true\n         case \"--warn\":\n             opts.warn = true\n         case \"--quiet\":\n             opts.quiet = true\n         case \"--status\":\n             opts.status = true\n         default:\n             return false, 0\n         }\n         return true, 1\n     }\n     \n     func parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) int {\n         for _, ch := range flags {\n             switch ch {\n             case 'b':\n                 opts.binary = true\n             case 't':\n                 opts.binary = false\n             case 'c':\n                 opts.check = true\n             case 'w':\n                 opts.warn = true\n             }\n         }\n         return 1\n     }\n     ```\n   \n   - `pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go` (READ - shared library providing DigestFiles, VerifyChecksums, FormatGNU, etc.):\n     - Important for understanding the API that sha256sum will call\n     - Key functions: `DigestFiles(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int`, `VerifyChecksums(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error)`\n     - Handles stdin via \"-\" filename, opens files, computes digests, formats output\n\n   - `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` (TO BE CREATED):\n     - Must be structurally identical to md5sum/main.go\n     - Changes: `crypto/sha256` import, `Algorithm: \"SHA256\"`, `NewHash: sha256.New`, `DigestLen: 32`, error prefix `\"sha256sum:\"` instead of `\"md5sum:\"`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The task was interrupted before any code was written.\n\n5.